## REQUIREMENT 5 – Repair and improve graph plotting functionality

### Current problem

The graph plotting functionality needs improvement so the resulting analysis can be examined properly.

I specifically require positive-valued graph representations, including absolute-value representations of the plotted quantities.

### Required implementation

Inspect the existing graphing code and determine why graph plotting is incomplete or unsuitable.

Implement reliable plotting of the available tracking and 3D kinematics data.

At minimum, provide:

- X-coordinate versus time.
- Y-coordinate versus time.
- Z-coordinate versus time.
- Velocity versus time.
- Acceleration versus time.
- Speed versus time.
- Other existing kinematic quantities supported by the application.

### Absolute-value graph functionality

Provide an explicit graph display option:

1. Signed values.
2. Absolute values.
3. Vector magnitude, wherever applicable.

For example:

- X-coordinate: x(t)
- Absolute X-coordinate: |x(t)|
- Y-coordinate: y(t)
- Absolute Y-coordinate: |y(t)|
- Z-coordinate: z(t)
- Absolute Z-coordinate: |z(t)|

The absolute-value mode must transform the plotted signal so that its displayed values are non-negative.

Important mathematical distinction:

- |x(t)| is the absolute value of the X-coordinate.
- |y(t)| is the absolute value of the Y-coordinate.
- |z(t)| is the absolute value of the Z-coordinate.
- Position magnitude is sqrt(x² + y² + z²).

Do not confuse an individual signal's absolute value with the 3D vector magnitude.

### Graph interface and behaviour

Provide:

- Clearly labelled horizontal and vertical axes.
- Time or frame-based horizontal axis.
- Units.
- Graph legend.
- Selection of plotted quantities.
- Signed/absolute-value/magnitude selection where applicable.
- Appropriate scaling.
- Data-point inspection or tooltips.
- Consistent graph updates as tracking progresses.
- Correct handling of missing, rejected, or interpolated tracking observations.

Graph updates must not destroy, modify, or reset tracking data.

Do not replace unavailable scientific data with artificial zeros merely to make a continuous graph.

The graph should be linked to the underlying tracking dataset, not to temporary UI state.

