# 5. Acceptance criteria

The work is not complete merely because the interface looks correct.

The following conditions must be satisfied:

- Camera 1 and Camera 2 can be played independently.
- Both cameras can also be played synchronously.
- Different video frame rates are handled correctly.
- The user can select the initial synchronization pair n ↔ m.
- Corresponding frames continue to be selected using media time.
- Both camera clip configurations are visibly and functionally independent.
- Camera 1 and Camera 2 have separate calibration-stick configurations in the 3D workspace.
- Existing graph plotting works correctly.
- Absolute-value plots are available without changing the underlying signed data.
- 3D vector magnitude is calculated separately from absolute coordinate values.
- Refreshing or switching between 2D and 3D does not silently destroy tracking observations.
- Replacing one source video does not destroy the other camera's data.
- Project saving and reopening work reliably.
- Existing functionalities and tests remain intact.

Do not claim that a requirement is complete unless the actual implementation and a corresponding test or reproducible manual verification support that claim.

